      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-9180-1",
        "name": "USN-9180-1",
        "description": "Albert Yang and Quang Luong discovered that the Compiler component of CRaC JDK 25 did not correctly handle certain inputs. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-114938)  It was discovered that the JGSS component of CRaC JDK 25 did not correctly authenticate users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114939)  Nicholas Carlini discovered that the JSSE component of CRaC JDK 25 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114940)  It was discovered that the Compiler component of CRaC JDK 25 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or to read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114941)  It was discovered that the Libraries component of CRaC JDK 25 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or to read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114942)  It was discovered that the Hotspot component of CRaC JDK 25 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114943)  Alexander Dezhinov, Stanislav Dukhin, Nikita Kozlov, and Binbin Xu discovered that the Core Java Libraries component of CRaC JDK 25 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114944)  It was discovered that the Libraries component of CRaC JDK 25 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114945)  It was discovered that the Compiler component of CRaC JDK 25 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114946)  Juraj Somorovsky, Maximilian Radoy, and Sven Hebrok discovered that the JSSE component of CRaC JDK 25 did not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114947)  In addition to security fixes, the updated packages contain bug fixes, new features, and possibly incompatible changes.  Please see the following for more information: https://openjdk.org/groups/vulnerability/advisories/2026-11-17",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2026-114938",
          "CVE-2026-114939",
